’re properly caffeinated\nand ready to handle some advanced math and code examples!","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"L7KG6oA2tp"}],"key":"RKZfpfy4aC"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exercises","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"pUcuGKIQIA"}],"identifier":"exercises","label":"Exercises","html_id":"exercises","implicit":true,"key":"bnCoHJlgHL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each week I will prepare 5–10 exercises related to the reading material for that week.\nThere are already some exercises in v0.93 of the book,\nbut over the next few months,\nI’ll be beefing up the exercises for each section,\nand preparing solutions for them,\nwhich I’ll provide for you each week.","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"key":"D1XXSRnfqj"}],"key":"TGIrpUN5G7"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The goal for the exercises is not to be hard:\nthey are just spot-checks to make sure you’re on board with the new material.\nIt’s important that you try to solve these exercises on your own:\ndon’t just look at them as a spectator!","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"SUuUpYhMxX"}],"key":"GcKf2yPZI0"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Office hours","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"key":"atMONDX69t"}],"identifier":"office-hours","label":"Office hours","html_id":"office-hours","implicit":true,"key":"sHhfcSwTJo"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":9